 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f86dfac1-59d9-4e0f-bf1e-77c0fc7b8c79"],
 " (the default) all of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"32ee00c8-029a-4817-9d63-cc5168cf5a29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The shell of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " about ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e62c39d-13bc-4521-9883-6e88b72c7d2d"],
 " \[LongDash] the sphere of the graph metric, as a vertex ",
 StyleBox["set",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f631d35-3a5f-4641-971e-05cb3742874c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is the discrete analogue of a sphere, not of a circle: it is \
codimension-1 as a set, but on a lattice its vertices are pairwise \
non-adjacent, so it carries no cycle. The cyclic object is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/FindInfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "27207222-146a-4426-a6ab-fc0e01f94095"],
 ", which needs a thickened band for exactly that reason."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2279fb82-8ab5-46f3-8007-4eda8dbd5582"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The shell is the substrate of the volume-growth invariants. Its cardinality \
as a function of ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " is the surface-area profile, and on a flat lattice it grows ",
 StyleBox["linearly",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", which is the statement that the dimension is 2. The slope is a property \
of the tiling: 4 per step on the square grid, 3 on the hexagonal."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b3d21ccd-5ef8-4b1d-afc6-a6cc9f785b1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["Properties"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09709a78-e70c-4ad7-82d3-52272b11d0d5"],
 " takes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e143d32-6ce3-4b1a-8b7d-9fea11a14713"],
 " (default; the whole level set as one realisation), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "\"\<Separating\>\"", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cdeab2e3-90fd-4021-88cc-705e66075044"],
 " (inclusion-minimal subsets separating the centre from beyond), or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Separating\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Connected\>\""}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f14e16e0-58bf-4d2e-a3be-0a02a99977c6"],
 ". Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77662a69-2c81-496f-8564-ed51a4551cc7"],
 " takes ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Exhaustive\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cfabf2e6-f65f-4474-bb95-6e0acb12c928"],
 " (default) or ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Greedy\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6833f12-fb52-4d47-b3ae-2f7dd84e98ea"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Volume\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b05772c-060f-44a0-80ac-52f27803d4b0"],
 " accessor gives the per-realisation vertex count as a list."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"845d25dc-8fdd-4838-8271-42f54e26119c"],

